                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I have no idea why the reviews for this game are mixed. Purgatory is a turn based RPG with a skill tree system, a decent amount of enemy types, great music, a compelling story, and a decent amount of levels. You cannot do much better on steam for 99 cents. The main issues that people seem to have with this game is the balancing, the shortness of the game, grinding, and the lack of enemy types. First of all, the balancing does have major issues, but only if you take the time to grind and level up the main character, Xzus, a ton. If you play the game the way it was meant to be played, pushing through the levels with the troops you have earned , forming a formation and strategy and attacking the enemies, then this game is balanced perfectly. If you want a challenging and fun experience, do not grind on the first couple levels until you have mexed out the skill tree. Another issue people seem to have is the shortness of the game. I think this is one of the best criticisms a game can have, since it means that you wanted more of the game. Anyways, this game only cost 99 cents, and thinking that you would get a ton of time out of it is idiotic. The game takes ~5 - 10 hours to beat depending on how you play it. For 99 cents, this is more that acceptable. Another apparent problem people say is that you must grind in this game. This game actually contains little to no grinding if you play the aforementioned way, pushing through with your current troops instead of farming easy battles. The final problem i have seem people complain about is the lack of enemy types. This isn't that huge. Though you dont face new enemy types every battle, the game throws new ones at you from time to time. I do get this complaint, but its not a massive deal.\n\n\nOVERALL\n\nOne of the best games you can get on steam for 99 cents IMO\nGreat Story\nGreat Music\nGreat Art\nDecent Gameplay\n\nFOR ITS COST it is very good would reccomend",
